Title: 0012-aros-keymap-rawkey-from-scancode
Repository: grafx2
Base-Commit: f84cb09dc59d706d6e7b28778b01ba911f52298c
Requires: 0011-aros-keymap-text-fallback.patch
Author: aros-grafx2 project
Date: 2026-10-08
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: AROS SDL2 text fallback in src/keyboard.c only (Keysym_to_ANSI under __AROS__). Replaces the raw-key lookup of patch 0011.

Problem:
  Patch 0011 rebuilt the AROS raw key from the SDL keycode. The AROS SDL2 backend (SDL 2.32.10 in the SDK) fills that keycode from the active keymap, so the keymap was applied twice: on QWERTZ z and y swapped, and every key whose unshifted character is above 0x7F (Italian ì ò à è, German ö ü) arrives as a negative keycode and was passed through as 0xFFxx. On the Italian keymap Shift+ì gave nothing instead of ^, Shift++ gave + instead of *, AltGr+ò gave nothing instead of @. Keys missing from 0011's keycode table fell back to the unshifted keycode.
Solution:
  Rebuild the raw key from the SDL scancode, which the backend takes positionally from a raw-key table (copied here). Use MapRawKey's result only when it is one printable Latin-1 character; control characters and CSI sequences keep the generic handling, a key with no character (lone modifier, dead key) or a control character produced with Ctrl gives 0, so Ctrl+letter inserts nothing (as in revision 4). KMOD_NUM no longer sets IEQUALIFIER_NUMERICPAD, which marks a keypad key rather than Num Lock. Keyboard shortcuts (Keysym_to_keycode) are unchanged.
Validation:
  Host: python3 tests/test-aros-keymap-text.py builds keyboard.c with
  __AROS__ against a MapRawKey stand-in carrying rows of pc104_usa,
  pc105_i and pc105_d, and checks the raw-key table against the one read
  from the SDK's libSDL2.a: 56 failures on the 0011 code (13 key
  cases, 43 raw keys not mapped back to themselves), 0 on this one.
  Guest 2026-10-08, AROS One 1.3 x86_64 ABIv11, pool slot v11-2, QEMU TCG,
  ABIv11 SDK SDL 2.32.10: with SetKeyboard pc105_i the same physical keys
  typed into the Save-picture comment field gave aA++*yzA on revision 4
  and aAi^+*@oc*yzA (with i-grave, o-grave, c-cedilla) on this build,
  identical to the AROS Shell; with pc105_d, zyZ, o/u-umlaut and * as in
  the Shell. Probe logs show Keysym_to_keycode unchanged. Report:
  docs/attachments/2026-10-08-keyboard-layouts/REPORT.md.
Removal:
  Keep while AROS SDL2 does not emit SDL_TEXTINPUT. The scancode table
  must match the backend's; recheck it when the SDK's SDL2 changes.

